					<h3>New Exibit opened in Namatanai</h3>
					<p>Namatanai is a town on the island province of
						New Ireland in Papua New Guinea. It is the second largest settlement on the island
						and connected to the largest and provincial capital of Kavieng (264 km to the
						north-west) by the Boluminski Highway. In 2005, Namantanai was estimated to have a
						population of 1300 people. It is the seat of Namatanai Rural LLG.</p>
